# Bounded hierarchy prototype architecture / pending independent freeze

2026-08-27. Delegated leaf owns only this new prototype subtree and requested
handoff receipts. No new prototype code or execution precedes authentication of
the independent v5 freeze candidate. Historical v4 material is read-only.

## Proposed representation and admission

- Inherit the finite v4 constructor, immutable branch-local event/environment
  snapshots and derived byte spans; bind inherited model SHA256
  `f04c98a52967f904266660607b0ee2157518cf50d3da260a4aa2b47926c392a0`.
- Retain exactly the v4 ceilings: work/allocation 1,000,000 logical units each
  per model, depth 24, events 2048, candidates 32, input 32 ASCII bytes,
  static nodes 64, child arity 16, repeat count 32, capture groups 16.
- Admit any new occurrence tables, context records, traversal stacks, comparison
  work and retained references through the same model meter before allocation
  or traversal. These counters are not physical-memory or engine-safety proof.
- Keep eligibility separate: finite permissive supplied histories versus named
  conditional LOCAL-TAIL-HYPOTHESIS. No new tail suppression or lossy merging.
- Implement at most two independently frozen hierarchy variants, with at most
  twelve frozen witness/control groups; retain required lifetime/cap/abort checks.
- Root P/aaa completed `a` is a target, not authority to alter eligibility or
  spans. TEMP D/abab retention deliberately differs from explicit Issue8.

## Definition blocker

The v4 review identifies repeat aggregate extent versus chronological BODY
priority, capture-wrapper aliasing, and initial absence versus END as separate
decisions. Earlier HNODE/HTREE prose and C1 are not assumed mutually consistent.
The independent freeze must name these choices explicitly. Any refinement will
be recorded as a v5 DESIGN delta, not relabeled unchanged semantics.

The independent early checkpoint now explicitly identifies the contradiction:
literal aggregate-bearing NODE and TREE both prefer P/aaaa `[a][a][a]+a`
over `[aa]+aa`, whereas historical C1 requires the latter. The planned two
variants retain this failed target rather than silently changing precedence.
The checkpoint is reasoning only, not authorization to implement before seal.

For NODE, a possible bounded representation is a static semantic-node preorder
plus one context-delimited occurrence list per dynamic semantic parent. Capture
wrappers alias their body for ordering only; original capture events remain.
Earlier parent columns must agree before later context lists are compared;
context alignment uses structural order, never allocation identifiers. For TREE,
compare the whole current semantic occurrence before each ordered child subtree.
Zero occurrences and a list ending after participation need distinct comparison
branches. Both mechanisms must charge table storage and traversal/comparison
before work, including empty contexts; no uncharged array append or retained
Map entry. Final representation awaits exact frozen definitions and witnesses.

## Admission details to carry into implementation

Use the existing meter's `array`/`record` admission helpers rather than hidden
growing collections. A bounded static preorder can reserve at most 64 slots;
two-pass context collection counts before allocating exact occurrence lists.
Every pass visits charged dynamic occurrences, including transparent wrapper
traversal and empty-repeat context admission. A comparison must check ownership,
policy, context alignment and terminal preference under the same budget, even
when returning a tie. Failed builds retain their cumulative charges. No table
cache publication may expose a partially prepared acceptance on exhaustion.

The inherited runner used a distinct 50,000,000-unit harness ceiling; retain it
only for fixture loading, assertions, permutation storage and report assembly,
never as an increased per-model allowance. Budget relation/permutation work;
these are repeated checks of the same frozen histories, not new input coverage.
Bounded report serialization is separate from matcher/model state. Cancellation
checks can observe a synchronous cooperative abort, not service an event-loop
callback in the middle of synchronous computation. Exact reason identity matters.

## Evidence plan

Authenticate freeze receipts and Git blobs before implementation. Execute only
owned immutable archive/temp inputs, never a live source or dist overlay. Bind
the inherited model, exact patch, runner, freeze inventory and guarded source
hashes before/after. Default stdout; explicit captures use exclusive creation.
Preserve old author two failed predictions, independent six failures (46/52),
adapter 44/50 and historical137 as history/future obligations without reruns.
Seal an explicit-path atomic candidate commit and publish its receipt before
the longer report. No matcher, worker, native run, promotion or parity claim.
